{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Certain men, sons of worthlessness (בליעל) shall go out.</b> The expression בליעל: one who does not rise into the company of the Holy One, blessed be He; or בלי עול — without a yoke, that is, he does not accept the yoke of Torah but rather casts off from himself the yoke of the kingdom of heaven. <b>Men (אנשים)</b> — our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'men' and not women. <b>And they shall draw away the inhabitants of their city</b> — and not the inhabitants of another city. From here they said: it does not become a wayward city (עיר הנדחת) until men lead it astray, and until those who mislead it come from within it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:06.902052595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}